  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Further development of Ruzizi 3 hydropower project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The agreement falls under Norad&apos;s Enterprise Development for Renewable Energy (EDRE) Scheme. Norad&apos;s early-stage support mitigates IPS&#x2019;s risks associated with the development of the Ruzizi 3 hydropower project.

Supported activities under this agreement include Geotechnical Engineering, the procurement of an EPC Contractor, Environmental and Social Impact Assessment, Land Acquisition, and Financial Closing. Upon commissioning, Ruzizi 3 will have an installed capacity of 206 MW and an annual forecasted production of 1,168 GWh.

The target beneficiaries are the populations of Burundi, the Democratic Republic of Congo, and Rwanda, with the generated power to be shared equally among these three countries.</narrative>
  </description>
